{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/cats-senses-signals-and-daily-care/audio/main-f31fb9851e3e.mp3","durationSec":141.672,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.38,"text":"Cats use their ears, eyes, and whiskers to learn about the world."},{"start":3.38,"end":9.02,"text":"Hearing: Cats hear very high sounds that people may not hear, such as a mouse's squeak."},{"start":9.64,"end":12.52,"text":"Their ears can turn toward a sound and help them find it."},{"start":12.52,"end":18.72,"text":"Low-light vision: A cat's eye has a special layer called the tapetum lucidum."},{"start":19.24,"end":21.32,"text":"It reflects light inside the eye."},{"start":22.08,"end":26.62,"text":"This helps cats see in very low light, but cats cannot see in complete darkness."},{"start":27.88,"end":30.6,"text":"Whiskers: Whiskers give a cat touch information."},{"start":31.28,"end":35.48,"text":"They help the cat notice nearby objects, judge spaces, and keep its balance."},{"start":36.82,"end":39.16,"text":"Cat body language shows how a cat feels."},{"start":40.08,"end":45.06,"text":"Look at the ears, eyes, whiskers, tail, and whole body together."},{"start":46.42,"end":48.72,"text":"Relaxed cat: The ears point forward."},{"start":49.3,"end":50.92,"text":"The eyes are soft or half closed."},{"start":51.54,"end":53.06,"text":"The whiskers rest near the face."},{"start":53.8,"end":56.56,"text":"The body is loose, and the tail may stand upright."},{"start":57.14,"end":58.52,"text":"This cat feels safe."},{"start":58.52,"end":61.4,"text":"Curious cat: The ears and whiskers point forward."},{"start":61.86,"end":62.68,"text":"The eyes are open."},{"start":63.16,"end":64.82,"text":"The cat may move toward something new."},{"start":65.1,"end":66.4,"text":"Its tail may stand up."},{"start":67.2,"end":70.26,"text":"Stressed cat: The ears turn sideways or lie flat."},{"start":70.66,"end":71.5,"text":"The eyes are wide."},{"start":71.88,"end":74.26,"text":"The body may crouch, and the cat may hide."},{"start":74.92,"end":79,"text":"Together, these signs are a stress signal that the cat needs quiet space."},{"start":79.5,"end":81.52,"text":"Simple daily care helps a cat stay comfortable."},{"start":82.1,"end":85.34,"text":"Fresh water: Give fresh, clean water at all times."},{"start":85.34,"end":87.62,"text":"Wash and refill the water bowl every day."},{"start":87.62,"end":91.14,"text":"A water fountain is optional; a clean bowl also works."},{"start":91.98,"end":94.62,"text":"Safe interactive play: Give the cat interactive toys."},{"start":95.18,"end":99.52,"text":"A wand toy lets the cat follow a moving toy while your hands stay away from its claws."},{"start":100.54,"end":102.34,"text":"Scratching: Cats need to scratch."},{"start":103.18,"end":105.8,"text":"Scratching removes the old outer cover from their claws."},{"start":106.38,"end":109.66,"text":"Give the cat a sturdy scratching post that does not wobble."},{"start":110.12,"end":114.02,"text":"Clean litter: Put the litter box in a quiet place that the cat can reach."},{"start":114.72,"end":117.66,"text":"Scoop solid waste from it at least once a day."},{"start":118.3,"end":122.82,"text":"A quiet sleep place: Give the cat a clean, dry place to rest."},{"start":123.5,"end":126.82,"text":"A soft, warm blanket or towel makes a simple bed."},{"start":127.58,"end":128.76,"text":"Wash the bedding often."},{"start":130.16,"end":136.92,"text":"Veterinary care: A cat should see a veterinarian at least once a year, and at once if it is sick or hurt."},{"start":138,"end":141.3,"text":"A veterinarian can give advice for the cat's age and health."}],"words":[{"text":"Cats","start":0,"end":0.26},{"text":"use","start":0.26,"end":0.52},{"text":"their","start":0.52,"end":0.74},{"text":"ears","start":0.74,"end":1.04},{"text":"eyes","start":1.32,"end":1.52},{"text":"and","start":1.74,"end":1.86},{"text":"whiskers","start":1.86,"end":2.26},{"text":"to","start":2.26,"end":2.48},{"text":"learn","start